      "title": "Home | Mueller Lab - Salk Institute for Biological Studies",
      "headings": [],
      "text": "Welcome to the Mueller lab What we do We study a mutually beneficial relationship between plant roots and soil fungi called arbuscular mycorrhiza symbiosis. More specifically, we study the molecular basis of plant control over symbiosis initiation and maintenance. Read more » Who we are We are an international team of scientists interested in symbiosis research, molecular biology, genetics, and plant physiology. Read more »",
